      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: `ExpandModules` only returns targets that have a `module_type` (i.e. C++ modules, like Swift modules or targets with `modulemap` configured). For standard targets without module maps (`module_type().none() \u003d\u003d true`), `ExpandModules` will silently drop them and return an empty list, causing `Exposes` to always return `false`.\n\nSince `gn suggest` is a general tool and should work on any target regardless of whether C++ modules are enabled, you should implement a simple graph traversal here instead of using `ExpandModules`.\n\nFor example:\n```cpp\nbool Exposes(const Target\u0026 target, const Target\u0026 underlying) {\n  if (\u0026target \u003d\u003d \u0026underlying)\n    return true;\n\n  std::vector\u003cconst Target*\u003e stack \u003d {\u0026target};\n  std::unordered_set\u003cconst Target*\u003e visited;\n\n  while (!stack.empty()) {\n    const Target* current \u003d stack.back();\n    stack.pop_back();\n\n    if (!visited.insert(current).second)\n      continue;\n\n    auto add_deps \u003d [\u0026](const LabelTargetVector\u0026 deps) {\n      for (const auto\u0026 pair : deps) {\n        if (pair.ptr \u003d\u003d \u0026underlying)\n          return true;\n        stack.push_back(pair.ptr);\n      }\n      return false;\n    };\n\n    if (add_deps(current-\u003epublic_deps()))\n      return true;\n\n    if (current-\u003eoutput_type() \u003d\u003d Target::GROUP) {\n      if (add_deps(current-\u003eprivate_deps()))\n        return true;\n    }\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n```",
